-- what an accepted read-across argument has and a rejected one lacks, as a type: a measured property of
-- the substance, and the hazard as a function of that property rather than of the structure. Equality of
-- the property then transports the hazard, by nothing more than that the hazard is a function of it.
-- This is the group or category argument that ECHA accepts at 62% against the analogue approach's 38%:
-- the category names the property, and the resemblance of two structures names nothing.
ra-via-property : (q : Mol → Nat) → (f : Nat → Nat) → (M : Mol) → (N : Mol) → q M ≡ q N → f (q M) ≡ f (q N)
ra-via-property q f M N p = cong f p
